hadiths[32]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2840","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is a supplication for every Prophet. I intend"
"2841","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the same is true from this chain of transmission."
"2842","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the hadith that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Seventy thousand people from my Ummah will go to Paradise without reckoning\"""""
"2843","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi al-Judaa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “With the intercession of a man from my Ummah, more people than Banutamim will enter Paradise.” The people said: “Except you, O Messenger of Allah!” He said: “Yes, except me.”"
"2844","Masrooq, may God have mercy on him, said: I asked the mother of the believers, Sayyida Aisha, may God be pleased with her: What do you think about the saying of Allah: \The day the earth will be changed to the earth and the heavens...\"" (Ibrahim: 48/14)"
"2845","Sidi, may God have mercy on him, said: I once heard this verse from Marah (Hamdani): . . . . . ﴾» (Maryam: 71/19) asked the meaning: (i.e.: There is none of you who will not enter the Hellfire), Marah narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrated a hadith to him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All people will enter the Hellfire, then they will come out of it according to their deeds, so the first person will come out like a flash of lightning, then the second like the wind, and the third like the running of a fast horse. The fourth like a camel-rider, and the fifth like a man running, the sixth like a man walking.\"" 2846"""""
"2846","(Marfu' Hadith) Hajjaj ibn Minhal informed us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: ""Death will be brought in the form of a dun-colored ram. It will be placed between Paradise and Hell. It will be said: 'O people of Paradise,' so they will stretch their necks and look. And it will be said: 'O people of Hell,' so they will stretch their necks and look. And they will see that relief has come. Then it will be slaughtered, and it will be said: 'Eternity, no death.'"""""
"2847","Sayyidina Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) giving a sermon. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated this word again and again, even if all the people in the market were present in my place, they would have listened, and while saying this, the cloak of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell at his feet."
"2848","Bahz bin Hakeem narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There was a servant of Allah who did not believe in any religion. He said: Very good father! He said: I will not leave my property with you, unless I give you an order, then he took a promise from them, he said: When I die, take me in the fire and when I am burnt, then throw my ashes in the air. He said: \By my Lord! These boys did the same to him after he died. He was brought to his original state and presented before the Lord of the Worlds. Allah Almighty said: What prompted you to take fire? He said: Your fear"
"2849","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A woman went to Hell because of a cat. It was said to her"
"2850","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Ninety-nine dragons will be imposed on the unbeliever in his grave"
"2851","Muhammad bin Wasee said: I went to Bilal bin Abi Barda, I said: Your father narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is a valley in Hell called Habhab"
"2852","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But those who are in Hell (i.e. are destined to stay there forever, like infidels and polytheists), they will not die in Hell, and some of the people will be such (disobedient) that the fire will catch them according to their sins and they will burn in it until they become coals, then they will be ordered to intercede, so they will be removed from Hell in groups. They will come out and spread in the rivers of Paradise, and it will be said to the people of Paradise: Pour water on them.\ He said: \""So the people of Paradise will pour water on those who come from Hell"
"2853","On the authority of Sayyidina Abdullah bin Masoud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There are eight gates to Paradise.\"""""""
"2854","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who goes to Paradise will enjoy himself"
"2855","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \In Paradise"
"2856","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: We asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): How is Paradise built? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \A brick of gold and a brick of silver"
"2857","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qays narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are four Jannahs of Al-Firdus, two Jannahs of gold, they and their ornaments (ornaments) and vessels and whatever is in them are all of gold, and two Jannahs of silver, their ornaments, vessels and everything are of silver, and there in the Jannahs of Eden there will be only a veil of gravel on the face of Allah between the people and the sight of Allah, and these rivers and jinns. It originates from Aden and later falls into the canals through pits.” \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Juba, by which the journey of the earth can be completed."
"2858","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The first group of my ummah who will enter Paradise will have faces as bright as the fourteenth moon"
"2859","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira and Sayyidna Abu Saeed (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): . . . . . . .﴾» (Al-A'raf: 43/7) Translation: (And they will be called that this paradise has been given to you in return for your deeds), the meaning of this verse is that they will be called and said: It has been decreed for you to be healthy, and you will never get sick, enjoy luxury, you will not have any sorrow and grief, stay young, do not grow old and live forever, never die."
"2860","Sayyidna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A man in Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating"
"2861","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The people of Paradise are bald men with gray hair"
"2862","On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, Abu Asim was asked: Did he narrate it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, the people of Paradise will neither urinate nor sneeze nor defecate, instead they will burp, eat, drink and will be inspired by Tasbeeh and Tahamid like the inspiration of breath."
"2863","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Allah"
"2864","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The lowest level of Paradise will be the one who wishes to Allah and it will be said to him: You have as much as you wished for and more like it"
"2865","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The people of Paradise will see the people of one upper room and the other upper rooms as you see the star in the sky (i.e. they will be so high and far from each other due to the difference in degrees).\"" Narrated and they said: As you see the Kukab Dari in the sky on the eastern or western edge."""""
"2866","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever goes to Paradise will have two wives"
"2867","On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qays, his father said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \In Paradise there will be a tent of hollow pearl"
"2868","On the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a believer wishes for a child in Paradise"
"2869","Sulaiman bin Barida, I believe, narrating from his father, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There will be one hundred and twenty rows of the people of Paradise"
"2870","Hakeem bin Muawiya narrated from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \In Paradise there is a sea of milk"
"2871","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: When “Inna Aatinaka Al-Kawthar” was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “It is a river of Paradise, the banks of which are made of gold, it flows on pearls and rubies, its soil is more fragrant than musk, and its taste is sweeter than honey, and its water is whiter (and transparent) than snow.”"
